Because these are commented out, every time you resize the window, the `CompositorEffect` allocates *new* compute pipelines, but the old ones are permanently left dangling in VRAM. **You must uncomment those two lines to actually stop the memory leak.**

**2. True Alpha Blending is Impossible**
In your `gsplat_render.glsl`, you are outputting the `final_depth` variable into the Alpha channel of your render texture. 
Because the Alpha channel is currently occupied by your depth data, you are completely throwing away the accumulated transparency (`t`) of the Gaussian Splats! This means the splats cannot softly blend with the Godot background; they render as opaque blocks. This perfectly matches your old `main.gdshader` (which was also rendering opaque), but to get beautiful, soft edges, you will eventually need to output the depth to a completely separate `r32f` texture.

